        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b79210f5-7513-320d-afb1-5700a5ff735d",
                "word": "sophisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d122d6fa-0755-4693-ba96-242d9fd36465",
                        "entry_id": "b79210f5-7513-320d-afb1-5700a5ff735d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sophismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "170dac36-e252-3f1e-8345-c697ed42f17d",
                        "entry_id": "b79210f5-7513-320d-afb1-5700a5ff735d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Raisonnement qui n’est logique ou vrai qu’en apparence, mais qui est délibérément conçu pour tromper ou faire illusion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rhetoric"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a2a8459-49e6-4f07-a583-4b4734b2a0b9",
                                "sense_id": "170dac36-e252-3f1e-8345-c697ed42f17d",
                                "text": "[…] le sophisme du progrès et l'illusion de croire à l'avenir de l'homme !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c92def0-a258-49c4-8abb-0d0eea7847f3",
                                "sense_id": "170dac36-e252-3f1e-8345-c697ed42f17d",
                                "text": "Dans ce point de vue, on apercevra que les raisonnements que l’on vient d’exposer ne sont que des sophismes frivoles, ou un badinage de l’esprit, fort déplacé dans l’examen d’une matière si importante."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8873c24c-b790-48ce-8974-4ab043977d19",
                                "sense_id": "170dac36-e252-3f1e-8345-c697ed42f17d",
                                "text": "Le sophisme que je combats dans cet écrit est d’autant plus dangereux, appliqué aux travaux publics, qu’il sert à justifier les entreprises et les prodigalités les plus folles. Quand un chemin de fer ou un pont ont une utilité réelle, il suffit d’invoquer cette utilité. Mais si on ne le peut, que fait-on ? On a recours à cette mystification : « Il faut procurer de l’ouvrage aux ouvriers. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "046dc93a-3d14-4cbb-b63f-ea91bb7c04db",
                                "sense_id": "170dac36-e252-3f1e-8345-c697ed42f17d",
                                "text": "Ce caractère de nécessité historique donne au mouvement antipatriotique actuel une force qu'on chercherait vainement à dissimuler au moyen de sophismes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30e56e5d-43eb-4893-81cd-a0e6ee788b4e",
                                "sense_id": "170dac36-e252-3f1e-8345-c697ed42f17d",
                                "text": "Ces docteurs confondent, par un grossier sophisme, un idéal qui, en tant que non changeant, peut par pure métaphore être qualifié de mort, avec les hommes, les êtres charnels qui embrassent cet idéal, lesquels, en cet embrassement, peuvent être si peu morts qu’ils se battront avec acharnement pour le défendre."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdb64ba2-acda-4d26-a45f-338b9f6504ac",
                                "sense_id": "170dac36-e252-3f1e-8345-c697ed42f17d",
                                "text": "J'avais dénoué cent fois ce sophisme, en montrant que le ressort des guerres n'était pas tant l'intérêt que l'honneur ; chose bien aisée à comprendre pour des hommes qui présen­tement risquaient tout, avec une faible chance de gagner, et de gagner fort peu."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c0547dd-4df0-3bbd-baad-fd8d325ea088",
                        "entry_id": "b79210f5-7513-320d-afb1-5700a5ff735d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tout raisonnement logique ou vrai qu’en apparence, qu'il soit exprimé avec bonne foi (paralogisme) ou dans le but de tromper (vrai sophisme)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "common"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b6a8d4c7-c9a2-449f-94f4-36bb329ea225",
                        "source_entry_id": "b79210f5-7513-320d-afb1-5700a5ff735d",
                        "target_lang_word": "Sophisma",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sophisma",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a39d46eb-7619-3407-ba2e-2168b5140789",
                                        "entry_id": "ab4682a1-7139-3322-8f9f-5cb188fa012a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ausgeklügelter Trugschluss"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37106d3d-4aea-470d-b3a6-e2527a936c39",
                                                "sense_id": "a39d46eb-7619-3407-ba2e-2168b5140789",
                                                "text": "„Er spürte, daß das ein Sophisma war, ein tollkühner Trugschluß, aber er hatte nicht den Willen, ihn zu entwirren, und klammerte sich an die Wahrheit, welche die Sätze an der Oberfläche besaßen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed2aad3b-1c04-4d22-868e-f1465f1208a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "b79210f5-7513-320d-afb1-5700a5ff735d",
                        "target_lang_word": "Sophismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sophismus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb29686d-e3d4-3ce7-87b5-e5a1ead9c474",
                                        "entry_id": "5ea5156c-c93b-394e-833b-58ed7e55ad11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "sophistische Argumentation oder eine bewusste Täuschung intendierender Trugschluss in der Argumentation"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2231d67-a58c-4c81-be92-099b7fde615a",
                                                "sense_id": "cb29686d-e3d4-3ce7-87b5-e5a1ead9c474",
                                                "text": "Sophismus in jedweder Form, der Missbrauch des Denkens oder der Sprache zur spitzfindigen Rechthaberei, weckten die Gegnerschaft eines Sokrates und Plato gegen die sogenannten griechischen Aufklärer."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "afe9a7f7-37bf-44a1-9ea3-60fb68d8c3ff",
                        "source_entry_id": "b79210f5-7513-320d-afb1-5700a5ff735d",
                        "target_lang_word": "sophism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sophism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac564dc1-c144-355c-9699-7d82cf1b73a3",
                                        "entry_id": "dd6de3b0-b63a-39ab-a69d-f4c063d239e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The school of the sophists in antiquity; their beliefs and method of teaching philosophy and rhetoric."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20afea1e-bed4-4525-8eda-324a071759ca",
                                                "sense_id": "ac564dc1-c144-355c-9699-7d82cf1b73a3",
                                                "text": "Within the framework of democracy a new ideology, born of sophism, took root and proclaimed the rights of the individual in all spheres, political as well as moral."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f0b141b-6926-4114-9fca-aa18ed014708",
                                                "sense_id": "ac564dc1-c144-355c-9699-7d82cf1b73a3",
                                                "text": "Empiricism has its roots in Greek and Roman sophism and skepticism, and continues through Kant and American pragmatism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a641a583-93f0-4f2e-9b36-735c80991453",
                                                "sense_id": "ac564dc1-c144-355c-9699-7d82cf1b73a3",
                                                "text": "Sophistic teachers did not, in general, consciously aim at corrupting the young or turning them against their parents, but the radical skepticism and moral relativism of later sophism indirectly achieved something like this."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27f0bdc2-c87e-346e-95b6-a434fa0086ca",
                                        "entry_id": "dd6de3b0-b63a-39ab-a69d-f4c063d239e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A flawed argument, superficially correct in its reasoning, usually designed to deceive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6407db2d-6031-4083-af81-fa154d6b6108",
                                                "sense_id": "27f0bdc2-c87e-346e-95b6-a434fa0086ca",
                                                "text": "The hope of improvement is a quality at once so strong and so excellent in the human mind, that I, for one, disapprove of any sophism—or, if you will, argument—that tends to repress it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae47ea99-238b-3882-85c3-68fea9c0182b",
                                        "entry_id": "dd6de3b0-b63a-39ab-a69d-f4c063d239e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An intentional fallacy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57eec020-ce2f-3cf5-8b6f-232d1c1f4450",
                                        "entry_id": "dd6de3b0-b63a-39ab-a69d-f4c063d239e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sophistic, fallacious reasoning or argumentation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1a2809e-cab4-471a-b312-ddf0803e5d27",
                                                "sense_id": "57eec020-ce2f-3cf5-8b6f-232d1c1f4450",
                                                "text": "What! No demonstration of the Being of God! No abstract arguments! No proofs a priori! Are these, which have hitherto been so much insisted on by philosophers, all fallacy, all sophism? Can we reach no further in this subject than experience and probability?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "501c6bcd-511e-4094-bcf4-892141b8d85e",
                                                "sense_id": "57eec020-ce2f-3cf5-8b6f-232d1c1f4450",
                                                "text": "30 Oct 1980, H. Dieter Zeh, letter to John Archibald Wheeler.\nI expect that the Copenhagen interpretation will some time be called the greatest sophism in the history of science, but I would consider it a terrible injustice if—when some day a solution should be found—some people claim that ‘this is of course what Bohr always meant’, only because he was sufficiently vague."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "974d1183-a23e-3b85-b919-0569740e9fbb",
                                        "entry_id": "dd6de3b0-b63a-39ab-a69d-f4c063d239e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wisdom and knowledge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
